                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "If Congress fails to act, 142,000 people in CT are facing skyrocketing health care costs. \n\nThe McShane family from Norwich, who owns a 20 year old small business, will see their premiums alone increase 115% by $12,000/year. That\u2019s not just unaffordable, it\u2019s impossible. \n\nOpen enrollment for Access health CT plans begins on Saturday. The clock is ticking for the GOP Congress to return to work and prevent this cost hike.",
